      "remediation": {
        "description": "WAF Web ACL does not have a parser limit protection rule, or the rule is not at the highest priority or is not in BLOCK mode. Requests that exceed parser limits bypass all subsequent rule evaluation silently.",
        "action": "Add a rule at the highest priority position (priority 0 or the lowest numeric value) that detects parser overflow and blocks the request. For Cloudflare, check http.request.headers.truncated == true. For AWS WAF, use a size constraint rule checking header count or total header size against the documented parser limit. The rule must be in BLOCK mode — COUNT mode detects but does not prevent the bypass. Verify the rule has higher priority than all managed rule groups and custom rules in the Web ACL.",
        "example": "{\n  \"waf\": {\n    \"kind\": \"web_acl\",\n    \"parser_limit_protection\": {\n      \"enabled\": true\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
      },
      "fix_plan": {
        "id": "fix-b6ed249cd83eb0f0",
        "target": {
          "asset_id": "arn:aws:wafv2::123456789012:webacl/prod-api",
          "asset_type": "aws_wafv2_web_acl"
        },
        "action": "Add a rule at the highest priority position (priority 0 or the lowest numeric value) that detects parser overflow and blocks the request. For Cloudflare, check http.request.headers.truncated == true. For AWS WAF, use a size constraint rule checking header count or total header size against the documented parser limit. The rule must be in BLOCK mode — COUNT mode detects but does not prevent the bypass. Verify the rule has higher priority than all managed rule groups and custom rules in the Web ACL."
